Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:24:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: /learn crashing with a server-side exception (and
 /learn/board/[id] would have crashed the same way the moment anyone clicked
 into a board)

Root cause: SearchableGrid ('use client') was being called from Server
Components (app/learn/page.tsx and app/learn/board/[id]/page.tsx) with
function props -- getKey, getSearchText, and especially renderItem
(which closes over BoardCard/VideoCard/EBookCard and returns JSX).
Functions aren't serializable across the Server -> Client Component
boundary in the App Router; only plain data and already-constructed
React elements are (the same way `children` always has been). Passing
a function prop like that throws at request time with "Functions
cannot be passed directly to Client Components" -- which is exactly
the server-side exception being reported, on every page using this
pattern.

This didn't show up in `tsc --noEmit` or even a successful `next
build`, because it's a RUNTIME RSC restriction, not a type error --
and these pages are all `dynamic = 'force-dynamic'`, so they're never
statically rendered at build time either. It only ever surfaces on a
real request with a real session, exactly how it was actually found.

Fix: SearchableGrid's API now takes items already shaped as
`{ key, searchText, node }`, where `node` is the pre-rendered
<BoardCard>/<VideoCard>/<EBookCard> JSX built by the caller -- plain
serializable React elements, not a function. This is the exact same
shape components/EbooksSearch.tsx already used (which is why the
E-Book page never had this bug) -- SearchableGrid just needed to match
that pattern instead of trying to be generic via callbacks.

Updated all 4 call sites: app/learn/page.tsx, and all three in
app/learn/board/[id]/page.tsx (the leaf-board classes grid, the
leaf-board e-books grid, and the BoardListView helper used for
mid-tree board listings).

Not touched, worth a look when there's time: a stray root-level
`next.config` file (no .js extension) got committed alongside
next.config.js in the same push -- Next only reads next.config.js so
it's inert, but it's confusing clutter worth deleting.
